# 3D Visualization System — Master Implementation Plan

**Phase:** 5 of frontend-v2 implementation plan
**Status:** Draft v3 — cuboid/tet premise, universe model, picking, LOD, R3F, synced camera

---

## 1. Core Architectural Premises

### Premise 1: Cuboids vs Tetrahedra — Nothing Else Differs

FDM renders **cuboids** (instanced boxes from grid shape + spacing). FEM renders **tetrahedral boundary faces** (triangles from FMMT topology binary). This is the **only** difference. One adapter, two geometry builders, one renderer.

### Premise 2: Universe / Multi-Object Space

A simulation creates a Universe containing one or more objects (e.g., disk, waveguide) and optionally an airbox. The viewport must:
- Render each object as a distinct entity with per-object color
- Allow clicking on any face to identify which object/cell it belongs to
- Show airbox as a separate toggleable layer (some simulations have no airbox)
- Support visualization scopes: `full` / `magnetic` / `airbox` / `object` / `part` / `selection`

### Premise 3: Interactive Picking & Probing

R3F raycasting → `faceIndex` + `elementMarkers` → object ID + cell index → field value. This enables COMSOL/Paraview-style point probes and object selection directly in the viewport.

### Premise 4: Large Simulation LOD

Giant simulations (millions of cells) need density reduction:
- Backend `SamplingProfile` (quality / balanced / interactive / memory_saver)
- Backend `max_glyphs` and `max_points` budgets
- Client-side stride-based decimation for FDM cuboids
- Client-side glyph subsampling

### Premise 5: Wireframe = Mesh View

Wireframe is not just a "debug overlay" — it IS the mesh visualization for inspection. This is a first-class display mode, not an afterthought.

---

## 2. Key Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Render framework | React Three Fiber (R3F) | `frameloop="demand"`, automatic disposal, declarative scene graph, native picking |
| Camera model | Shared across all panes | User requirement: rotate in any pane, all rotate together |
| Per-pane config | Layer visibility + display mode only | Each pane shows different layers of the same scene |
| FDM/FEM split | Geometry builder only | Single renderer, two adapters produce `CellGeometryResult` |
| Picking | R3F `onPointerDown` + element markers | Object/face/cell identification from raycasting |
| LOD | Backend budgets + client stride/subsampling | Respect `SamplingVisualizationState` from backend |

